WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.930
So months ago, I told you that the White House
and Donald Trump are trying to normalize Corona

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.690
virus deaths so that they're just not notable
anymore.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.820
Yeah, people are dying.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.500
People are dying from Corona virus every day.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.170
But we're sort of moving on.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.730
And this is hard to pinpoint exactly when
it started.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:23.820
But certainly it was a very clear decision
that was made when Donald Trump wondered aloud

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:31.430
about injecting bleach and isopropyl alcohol
to treat Corona virus.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.370
That was where it was like very clear.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.380
These are really doing much more damage, these
press briefings, than they are helping anybody

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.850
in the Trump administration.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.500
And so they stop the daily press briefings
and they essentially considered that they

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.480
had defeated the invisible enemy, or as Donald
Trump often calls it, the invisible scorch.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.430
Trump stopped talking about it, talked exclusively
about the stock market reopening, how we've

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.400
won, and there's therapeutics and vaccines
on the way.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.989
We stopped seeing doctors, Foushee and Berk's
on any kind of regular basis.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.520
And Trump increasingly distanced himself from
the even medical claims that Dr. Foushee would

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.520
make.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.689
And one of the themes of the Trump administration,
bigger picture has been hyper normalization.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:16.860
And that's exactly what they're trying to
do with corona virus.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:23.469
Hyper normalization is the making normal of
things that should not be seen as normal,

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:28.929
including the weekly or near daily scandals
that we've seen during this administration,

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:34.079
the way in which Trump talks to people and
uses xenophobic and racist dog whistles and

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:37.880
has made fun of and bullied just about everybody.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.579
And I've admitted that even for me, because
I'm in this stuff and covering this stuff

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:47.329
every day, I have to go out of my way to remind
myself, even though 20 of these things happened

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:49.279
this week, none of them is normal.

00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:53.139
If any one of these things had happened during
Barack Obama's presidency, they would be one

00:01:53.139 --> 00:01:55.990
week scandals on Fox News.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.899
That gets us to the new reports coming out
of the White House.

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:03.939
And these are reports from people close to
the Trump campaign and the Trump administration.

00:02:03.939 --> 00:02:05.159
The new goal is and

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:10.599
it's of course, we knew this, they want to
reframe the corona virus.

00:02:10.599 --> 00:02:17.459
They want to make the exploding number of
cases and also the four now lower, but still

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:19.709
significant number of deaths.

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:22.670
The new normal make people numb to the numbers.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.599
If you hear that 400 people died every day.

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:31.920
Eventually it sort of becomes I hate to use
this analogy like kids dying of hunger in

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.920
Africa.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.920
Right.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.780
Eventually, it becomes not about the individuals.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.219
It becomes a number.

00:02:37.219 --> 00:02:38.629
And we're sort of used to the number.

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:43.780
There's gun violence and people die from from
gun, from gun violence.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.390
And we're not going to stop selling people
guns as the gun people have said.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.989
And people kids are dying of hunger in Africa
every day.

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.500
But we're still going to continue to throw
out 30 percent of our food or whatever it

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.500
is.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.500
Right.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.500
As the phrase

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.299
is, a phrase often goes and, you know, 400
people died of corona virus, but we're essentially

00:03:02.299 --> 00:03:04.810
numb to it is the goal from the Trump administration.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.090
And there's a reason that Donald Trump talks
about it less and less other than to claim

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:15.959
victory, which is his campaign realizes that
Corona virus is a loser of a topic for him.

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:21.689
This is one of the reasons why his approval
rating has imploded, his handling of the virus,

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:28.609
the associated economic handling, and recently
the reaction to the protests against police

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:29.609
brutality.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:37.290
So the focus will continue to be economic
recovery, jobs, CEOs, fast food restaurants

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:40.700
opening and make the cases and deaths.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.700
The new normal.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.260
We can live with the virus.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.480
Schools should reopen.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.850
That's a focus now.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.439
There should be professional sports.

00:03:47.439 --> 00:03:49.400
We'll have a vaccine any day now.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.670
Everybody should just keep doing more and
more stuff.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:57.280
Even if the case numbers keep increasing,
even if we're hitting weekly new case records

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.780
a week in and week out.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:03.829
And if we end up with an escalating death
toll that some expect in the next month, I'm

00:04:03.829 --> 00:04:12.530
going to have a bigger report tomorrow about
the increase in cases without yet an increase

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.689
in deaths.

00:04:13.689 --> 00:04:15.469
But we may still get that in the next month.

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:16.469
Hopefully we won't.

00:04:16.469 --> 00:04:22.480
But the Trump administration idea is if we
stop talking about it, if we stop highlighting

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.030
it, maybe Trump's.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.990
Base will at least move on and maybe the media
will start to move on.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:35.400
The idea is the public will accept 50000 cases
a day, maybe even 100000 cases a day if the

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.430
numbers go in that direction, because eventually
there will be a vaccine and a treatment.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.510
People will become numb to the numbers and
we've got to keep

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.510
the economy open.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:48.650
So my message to you is we can't let them
make that this story right.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.190
Trump has failed hugely on the virus.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.440
They are doing this.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.160
They're trying to normalize the rapid spread
of the virus because they recognize that the

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.650
virus could be what removes Donald Trump from
office in the November election.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.580
Trump's approval rating on dealing with Corona
virus is in the toilet.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:11.570
Voters overwhelmingly prefer Joe Biden to
Trump in terms of who would would Biden better

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:14.400
deal with Corona virus than Trump has?

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:20.180
If we could identify the one moment where
it really went bad, I keep going back to what

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:27.140
about if we hit the body with isopropyl alcohol
and bleach and then from there it's been very

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.000
much downhill.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.460
And if the numbers don't turn around.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.140
The only choice they have is let's normalize
it.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.460
Let's make people numb to

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.460
it.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.370
Let's make believe that this is just normal.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.390
And notice that we talk about that phrase.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:44.230
An ounce of prevention is cheaper than a pound
of cure.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:49.140
Simply dealing with the virus properly from
day one would have been both much simpler

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:55.840
and much less costly in terms of money and
lives than now trying to lie to people to

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.520
get them to vote for you.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.080
We would have saved lives.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.280
We would have almost seen a guaranteed Trump
reelection if Trump had handled it well.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.640
If Trump had actually dealt with Corona virus
starting on January 20th.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.960
Remember, South Korea got their first case
on January 20th.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.090
So did we.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.190
Maybe because of the time difference.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:18.550
It was the 19th and the 20th, but within hours
of each other, South Korea and the US got

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.980
our first cases.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.020
The US had low testing and high spread.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.020
Whereas South

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.750
Korea immediately developed test contact,
traced isolated people.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.930
We could have had high testing, lower spread,
fewer cases, fewer deaths.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.750
And it would be really tough for Joe Biden
right now.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:41.610
If Trump had demonstrated leadership by really
dealing with the virus, I don't know that

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:45.020
Biden's polling plus 12 nationally, if that's
the case.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.670
Prevention is cheaper than cure.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:51.300
Avoiding the situation, getting so bad to
begin with would have been way easier than

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.350
now, trying to fix it.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.920
And when I say fix it, I mean both electorally
and in terms of the virus.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:01.770
If you look at Florida, Texas and Arizona,
it's essentially out of control.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.400
You're looking now at months to reduce those
case numbers, just like it took that long

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.860
in Massachusetts and in New York and in other
places.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:13.960
So just a reminder, in 2014, when two Americans
died of Ebola.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.010
Republicans were demanding

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.660
Obama's head on a stick.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:21.010
We now have over one hundred and thirty thousand
deaths in the United States.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:26.640
And the Trump strategy is normalize it and
pretend that that's just the way things have

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.640
to be.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.090
And I cannot skip this important piece.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:31.560
Sorry I hit my might because I'm getting so
wound up.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:36.520
This goes back to the failures of the educational
system in the US and the cultural failures

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:40.900
as well, especially among the right when it
comes to anti intellectual ism.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:47.700
If you know even a little bit more about medicine,
science, statistics, critical thinking, epistemology,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:53.190
media literacy, a ton of the disinformation
that spreads about the virus would never spread.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:56.020
Some of it would, but a lot less of it would
spread.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:00.080
If you are slightly more educated, you don't
fall for record.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.740
Job creation in June, four point eight million
jobs.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:03.740
If you're slightly

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.210
more educated, you realize.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.420
Wait a second.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.760
We lost 47 million jobs.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.530
We got four point eight million back.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.300
We're really in bad shape.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.000
What the hell is Trump talking about?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.330
But unfortunately, people do fall for it.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.440
So part of this is education.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:22.090
Part of it is you have a willing audience
that wants to repeat anything that Trump says

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.860
for political reasons.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.240
And that's where we end up today.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.650
Now, very, very last thing.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:31.650
Even if Americans grow numb to the cases and
the deaths, I don't know that they will grow

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.630
numb to being evicted.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:38.090
I don't know that they will grow numb to not
having money to pay their bills or to not

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:39.140
having a job.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:09:00.350
So that is something that will be tougher
to normalize for the Trump administration.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:46.140
We'll just

00:09:46.140 --> 00:10:13.890
have 
to see how it goes.

